e? If a shard is invalid, statuses unknown → treat as planned. I'll ignore merge errors in check-defects (design doesn't list shard errors there).\n\n### platform-gate.mjs\nsatisfies(requires, opts?) with process.platform. For 'pwsh': look for pwsh in PATH (win32 → pwsh.exe). Node's process.env.PATH split by delimiter.\n\nrecordSkip({test, file, ac, requires, reason}) — appends JSON line to <CLIWORKER_RESULTS_DIR>/skips.jsonl if set.\n\nFields: schema:'cliworker.skip/v1', test, file, ac, requires, platform, node, reason, at.\n\nplatformTest(name, opts, fn): file required (import.meta.url). Convert to relative path from repo root (root = dirname of dirname of file? file is <repo>/test/... or fixture). Design says \"函数内部转成相对仓库根的 / 路径\". Use `path.relative(process.cwd(), fileURLToPath(file))`? Better: derive root from CLIWORKER_ROOT env if set else cwd. I'll use CLIWORKER_ROOT ?? process.cwd().\n\nImplementation:\n```js\nexport function platformTest(name, opts, fn) {\n  const { ac = null, requires, file, reason } = opts || {}\n  test(name, (t) => {\n    if (satisfies(requires)) return fn(t)\n    const why = reason || `requires ${requires} not satisfied on ${process.platform}`\n    recordSkip({ test: name, file: relPath(file), ac, requires, reason: why })\n    t.skip(why)\n  })\n}\n```\nNote t.skip() then return; per node:test, calling t.skip() marks skipped.\n\nA1-13 requires the literals 'cliworker.skip/v1', 'platformTest', 'recordSkip', 'satisfies' in the file. ✓\n\n### runner-selftest.test.mjs\nTests:\n[AC-001]:\n- enumeration excludes fixtures/helpers/perf, orphans\n- verifyFullRun four error kinds\n- run fixture ok full + filtered\n- check-test-discovery selftest exits 0\n- platformTest skip record format\n\n[AC-002]: check-ci mutations.\n\n[AC-003]: check-fast injection tests + pwsh platformTest.\n\nneed spawnSync helper with `process.execPath`.\n\nCareful: inside `npm test`, CLIWORKER_RUN_ACTIVE=1 and CLIWORKER_RESULTS_DIR=<dir>. Spawning run-tests without --out