ts which spawns node --test with cwd = fixture root; the nested guard: parent env has CLIWORKER_RUN_ACTIVE=1 when run under npm test; out-dir is a fresh mkdtemp → OK.\n\nWait, careful in step 2: we pass `--root <abs fixture path>`; manifest files relative to fixture root. Compare to ['test/flows/c.test.mjs','test/integration/b.test.mjs','test/unit/a.test.mjs'].\n\n### gen-ci.mjs renderCi\nLet me write it as a function building lines with explicit strings. Need `${{ ... }}` in output. Use single-quoted strings.\n\n```js\nexport function renderCi(matrix) {\n  const lines = []\n  lines.push('# generated by scripts/gen-ci.mjs from scripts/ci-matrix.json - do not edit')\n  lines.push('name: ci')\n  lines.push('on: [push, pull_request]')\n  lines.push('permissions:')\n  lines.push('  contents: read')\n  lines.push('jobs:')\n  lines.push('  check:')\n  lines.push('    strategy:')\n  lines.push('      fail-fast: false')\n  lines.push('      matrix:')\n  lines.push('        include:')\n  for (const os of matrix.os) for (const node of matrix.node) {\n    lines.push(`          - name: ${os.name}`)\n    lines.push(`            runs_on: ${os.runs_on}`)\n    lines.push(`            baseline: ${os.baseline}`)\n    lines.push(`            node: ${node}`)\n  }\n  ...\n```\nHmm, `baseline` in the matrix entry — extra but harmless; A2-03 doesn't care. Should I include? The matrix os entries have baseline; including it in the workflow matrix is noise. Skip baseline in YAML to keep minimal. Actually including unknown keys is harmless. I'll skip it (not required).\n\nNote: matrix `include` with `name` keys — `${{ matrix.name }}` works.\n\nThen:\n```\n    runs-on: ${{ matrix.runs_on }}\n    env:\n      CLIWORKER_RESULTS_DIR: ${{ github.workspace }}/test-results\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4\n        with:\n          node-version: ${{ matrix.node }}\n      - run: npm ci\n      - run: npm run check\n      - uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4\n        if: always()\n        with:\n          name: test-results-${{ matrix.name }}-node${{ matrix.node }}\n          path: |\n            test-results/files-executed.json\n            test-results/skips.jsonl\n          if-no-files-found: warn\n  perf:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    continue-on-error: true\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4\n        with:\n          node-version: 22\n      - run: npm ci\n      - run: npm run perf\n```\nUse `matrix.check_command` for the check run step and `matrix.results_dir` for paths and env. And `matrix.perf.*`.\n\nThe `path: |` block must use results_dir.\n\nTrailing newline at end (lines.join('\\n') + '\\n').\n\n`on: [push, pull_request]` — hmm A2-03 doesn't check. But `on` in YAML 1.1 could be parsed as boolean `true` key; GitHub accepts. Fine.\n\ngen-ci CLI: no args → write; --stdout; --root.\n\n### check-ci.mjs\n```js\nexport function checkCi({root}) → errors\n```\nSteps:\n1. read matrix: if parse fails → ci.matrix_invalid.\n2. validate: os names sorted equals ['macos','ubuntu','windows']; node array deep equal [20,22]; check_command === 'npm run check'; artifacts deep equal; perf.blocking === false.\n3. read ci.yml; missing → ci.missing.\n4. expected = renderCi(matrix); if actual !== expected → ci.stale.\n5. perf_blocking: check expected contains 'continue-on-error: true' under perf or 'needs: perf'. Since we generate it, this is a sanity check on renderCi output. Implement: if (!expected.includes('continue-on-error: true')) error; if (/needs:\\s*perf/.test(expected) || /\\n\\s+needs:/.test(expected)) → error. Hmm \"存在 needs: perf\". I'll check `/\\bneeds:/` ? Careful: \"或存在 needs: perf\". So only `needs: perf`. But A2-03 requires zero `needs:` occurrences in the file. Since renderCi never emits needs, fine. For step 5 I'll check `expected.includes('needs: perf')`.\n\nNote if matrix invalid we can't render → return early.\n\nOutput: `FAIL <id> <detail>` then `check-ci: FAILED (<n> errors)` exit 1; else `check-ci: ok` exit 0.\n\n### milestone-gate & check-defects share defects logic\ncheckDefects receives `index` (parsed). Returns { errors, absent }.\n\nLet me define:\n```js\nexport function checkDefects({ root, index, milestone }) {\n  const errors = []\n  const ledgerPath = path.join(root, 'test', 'characterization', 'defects.json')\n  if (!fs.existsSync(ledgerPath)) {\n    if (milestone) { errors.push({ id: 'defects.file_missing', detail: 'test/characterization/defects.json' }) }\n    return { errors, absent: true }\n  }\n  ...\n}\n```\nCLI: if absent && !milestone → print `check-defects: defects.json absent, nothing to check`, exit 0.\n\nSchema validation collects errors and continues where safe.\n\nThen required list.\n\n`allIds` for M5 set mismatch: \n```js\nconst EXPECTED = ['a1-quota','a2-pack','a3-runner','a4-paths','a4-null-config','a5-dup-call','a5-forecast-x3','a5-unused','a5-ignored-fields','a5-shell','a5-nocache']\n```\nCompare sorted sets.\n\nOutput lines: `FAIL <id> <id-of-defect> <detail>`.\n\nNow for `mergeShards` default-mode status: need { root, index } where index has `acs`.\n\n### platform-gate relative path\n`file: import.meta.url` → relPath. Use CLIWORKER_ROOT ?? process.cwd(). In tests we call recordSkip directly with a mkdtemp results dir.\n\nFor the [AC-001] platformTest test: call `platformTest` with requires 'nope'? satisfies only accepts known values; unknown → treat as false? Design: requires 取 win32|wsl|darwin|linux|pwsh|secret-tool|security. I'll make satisfies return false for unknown. Then the test becomes skipped (counts as skipped in the run, not fail). Hmm, but the test wants to assert recordSkip wrote a line — if the test body never runs, no assertion happens. Instead: directly call `recordSkip` and assert file contents. Design says: \"`platformTest` 在条件不满足时写出合规的 cliworker.skip/v1 记录（用 mkdtemp 目录与 CLIWORKER_RESULTS_DIR）\". So test: set env, run a tiny child process that imports platform-gate