{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b64f-ed43-7e74-ae42-4f50cc3ae893","session_id":"01a1b64b-fe4d-73dd-9fb2-26f680d0b3a8","message":{"id":"01a1b64fed437e74ae424f4eda607738","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now check-test-discovery.mjs.\n\nStructure:\n```js\nimport fs, os, path, { spawnSync }, { fileURLToPath }\n\nconst HERE, REPO_ROOT\n\nmain():\n  parse --root/--manifest\n  if root given → single point check\n  else → selftest\n```\n\nWait: design says `node check-test-discovery.mjs --root <dir> [--manifest <file>]` is single-point. And no args → full selftest. What if --root without --manifest? Then just orphan check.\n\nSingle point output: `FAIL <id> <path>` per error, exit 1. On success print `check-test-discovery: ok`? A1-09 only checks exit code & id match; printing ok is fine.\n\nHmm — but careful: A1-09's manifest-ok expects exit 0. Print ok.\n\nSelftest:\n```js\nfunction selftest() {\n  const failures = []\n  const note = (msg) => { failures.push(msg); process.stdout.write(`FAIL ${msg}\\n`) }\n```\n1. orphans(REPO_ROOT) empty; enumerated no excluded prefixes.\n2. run fixture ok full.\n3. drift manifests.\n4. orphan fixture.\n5. filtered run.\n\nFor running run-tests: `spawnSync(process.execPath, [path.join(HERE,'run-tests.mjs'), '--root', root, '--out-dir', tmp], { encoding: 'utf8' })`.\n\nNote: spawnSync stdio default 'pipe' captures child's output but the child's own child (node --test) inherits the child's stdio → piped → captured. Fine (not printed). Good for quiet output.\n\nBut careful: if run-tests fails, we might want details. Print stderr on failure.\n\ntmp dir: fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), 'cliworker-ctd-')).\n\nClean up at end with rmSync.\n\nExpected files for ok fixture: ['test/flows/c.test.mjs','test/integration/b.test.mjs','test/unit/a.test.mjs'].\n\nAlso verify manifest.mode === 'full'.\n\nDrift:\n```js\nconst drift = path.join(HERE, '..', 'test', 'fixtures', 'discovery-selftest', 'drift')\nconst enumerated = enumerateTestFiles(drift)\ncheck('manifest-ok.json', ['discovery.none'])\n```\nCompare error id sets:\n- ok: no errors\n- missing: has discovery.missing\n- extra: has discovery.unexpected\n- filtered: has discovery.mode_not_full\n\nFindOrphans(drift) is empty so no orphan errors.\n\nOrphan fixture: findOrphans includes 'test/loose.test.mjs'.\n\nFiltered run on ok fixture: exit 0, mode filtered, files length 1, files[0]==='test/unit/a.test.mjs'.\n\nFinally if failures → exit 1 (print summary), else print 'check-test-discovery: ok'.\n\nCareful about A1-08: `$r.Out -match 'check-test-discovery: ok'` → must print exactly.\n\nNow single-point mode also should print `check-test-discovery: ok`? Let's do it for consistency; A1-09 doesn't check text.\n\nHmm wait, one catch: in single-point mode with drift fixtures, findOrphans(drift) — the drift fixture's test/unit/a.test.mjs and b.test.mjs are enumerated → no orphans. ✓\n\nImplementation detail: for the full selftest, running run-tests on ok fixture while the parent is inside `npm test` (env CLIWORKER_RUN_ACTIVE=1, CLIWORKER_RESULTS_DIR=<outer>) → we pass --out-dir mkdtemp → guard passes. ✓\n\nBut careful: when check-test-discovery runs from check-fast (npm test step), same. ✓\n\nLet me write.\n\nAlso note \"1. 真实仓库：findOrphans(仓库根) 为空\" — this requires test/select.test.mjs gone. I'll flag that.\n\nWrite file.","signature":""}],"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b64c02387d24acacbd4a13028c46","_messageId":"01a1b64fed437e74ae424f4eda607738","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b64c02387d24acacbd4a13028c46","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b64fed437e74ae424f4eda607738","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b64fed437e74ae424f4eda607738","codebuddy