{"type":"user","uuid":"01a1b650-7d10-7af7-8c56-0a1f84b9493c","session_id":"01a1b64b-fe4d-73dd-9fb2-26f680d0b3a8","message":{"content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_00_6LY988KYVimX1vvdji1w0370","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully created and wrote to new file: c:\\git\\dsh-CLIWorker\\.collab\\worktrees\\001\\scripts\\check-ci.mjs"}],"is_error":false}],"role":"user"},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b64c02387d24acacbd4a13028c46","_messageId":"01a1b65065c87792aaac2f88e3b0f48a","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b64c02387d24acacbd4a13028c46","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b65065c87792aaac2f88e3b0f48a","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b65065c87792aaac2f88e3b0f48a","traceparent":"00-1491732b1efa8226a936b146e12cfead-98331ebc19389995-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a1b64b-fe4d-73dd-9fb2-26f680d0b3a8,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a1b64c02387d24acacbd4a13028c46"},"__timestamp":"2026-11-07T14:01:30.643Z"}
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b650-7d1e-7452-9592-7c7903466bdd","session_id":"01a1b64b-fe4d-73dd-9fb2-26f680d0b3a8","message":{"id":"01a1b6507d1e745295927c77c0e608ed","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now check-defects.mjs and milestone-gate.mjs.\n\ncheck-defects.mjs:\n\n```js\nimport fs, path, { fileURLToPath }\nimport { mergeShards } from './check-traceability.mjs'\n```\nCareful: importing check-traceability triggers its `invokedDirectly` check — false when imported. ✓\n\nDEFECT_IDS = 11.\n\n```js\nexport function checkDefects({ root, index, milestone }) {\n  const errors = []\n  const ledgerFile = path.join(root, 'test', 'characterization', 'defects.json')\n  let ledger\n  try { ledger = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(ledgerFile,'utf8')) }\n  catch { \n    if (fs.existsSync(ledgerFile)) errors.push({id:'defects.schema', detail:'ledger is not valid JSON'})\n    else if (milestone) errors.push({id:'defects.file_missing', detail:'test/characterization/defects.json'})\n    return { errors, absent: !fs.existsSync(ledgerFile) }\n  }\n```\nHmm careful: distinguishing parse failure vs missing.\n\n```js\n  if (!fs.existsSync(ledgerFile)) {\n    if (milestone) errors.push({id:'defects.file_missing', detail:'test/characterization/defects.json'})\n    return { errors, absent: true }\n  }\n  let ledger = null\n  try { ledger = JSON.parse(...) } catch { errors.push({id:'defects.schema', detail:'ledger is not valid JSON'}); return { errors, absent:false } }\n```\n\nThen:\n```js\n  const list = Array.isArray(ledger?.defects) ? ledger.defects : null\n  if (!list) { errors.push({id:'defects.schema', detail:'defects must be an array'}); return {errors, absent:false} }\n\n  const knownAcs = new Set((index?.acs ?? []).map(e => e.ac))\n  const ids = new Set()\n  const valid = []\n  for (const item of list) {\n    if (!item || typeof item !== 'object') { errors.push({id:'defects.schema', detail:'entry must be an object'}); continue }\n    const { id, owner_task, owner_milestone, ac } = item\n    const problems = []\n    if (typeof id !== 'string' || id === '') problems.push('id')\n    if (typeof owner_task !== 'string' || !/^T-\\d{3}$/.test(owner_task)) problems.push('owner_task')\n    if (!MILESTONES.includes(owner_milestone)) problems.push('owner_milestone')\n    if (typeof ac !== 'string' || !knownAcs.has(ac)) problems.push('ac')\n    if (problems.length) { errors.push({id:'defects.schema', detail:`${id ?? '-'} missing or invalid: ${problems.join(',')}`}); continue }\n    if (ids.has(id)) { errors.push({id:'defects.schema', detail:`duplicate id ${id}`}); continue }\n    ids.add(id)\n    valid.push(item)\n  }\n```\n\nThen set mismatch for M5.\n\nThen determine required:\n```js\n  let required\n  if (milestone) required = valid.filter(d => milestoneRank(d.owner_milestone) <= milestoneRank(milestone))\n  else {\n    const merged = mergeShards({ root, index })\n    required = valid.filter(d => merged.acs[d.ac] === 'covered')\n  }\n```\nThen for each required check file:\n```js\n  for (const d of required) {\n    const file = path.join(root,'test','characterization','defects',`${d.id}.test.mjs`)\n    let source = null\n    try { source = fs.readFileSync(file,'utf8') } catch { source = null }\n    const hasFixed = source !== null && extractTitles(source).some(t => t.kind === 'plain' && t.title.startsWith('[fixed]'))\n    if (!hasFixed) errors.push({id:'defects.missing_fixed', detail:`${d.id} has no [fixed] section`})\n  }\n```\nOutput format: `FAIL <标识> <id> <说明>` → `FAIL defects.missing_fixed a5-shell has no [fixed] section`.\n\nCLI:\n- --milestone, --root, --index\n- milestone validation → exit 2 if invalid\n- read index (required for ac check). If index missing → index.* not our concern; use empty index? If index can't be read, `ac` validation would flag everything. I'll read index; on failure use `{acs: []}` and push a defects.schema? Better: exit 2? Design doesn't say. Keep simple: if unreadable, use { acs: [] } → defects.schema for every entry. Hmm. In practice index exists.\n\nActually for the fixture roots, index is at <root>/contracts/spec/ac-index.json. Default index = path.join(root,'contracts','spec','ac-index.json'). For A74-04/05 fixtures, that exists. ✓\n\n- default & absent → print `check-defects: defects.json absent, nothing to check`, exit 0.\n- else print errors → ok / FAILED.\n\nA74-05 M9 → exit 2. ✓\n\nmilestone-gate.mjs:\n\n```js\nexport function milestoneGate({ root, index, milestone }) → errors\n```\nSteps as designed. Needs spawn run-tests. In gate, `RUN_TESTS = path.join(HERE,'run-tests.mjs')`.\n\nFor the run, use spawnSync to keep it simple (gate CLI is sync). spawnSync(process.execPath, [RUN_TESTS, '--root', root, '--out-dir', tmp], { cwd: root, encoding: 'utf8' }).\n\nWait: run-tests resolves --root relative to cwd; we pass absolute root. ✓\n\nAfter: status !== 0 → gate.run_failed. Read manifest.\n\nThen for each index entry with milestone <= Mx and status covered: files from shards. But mergeShards returns only statuses, not files! I need files per AC.\n\nHmm. Design step 4: \"属主里程碑 <= Mx 的所有 covered 条目引用的文件，有不在 files 里的：gate.file_not_executed\". So the gate needs the file lists. mergeShards doesn't return them.\n\nOptions: extend mergeShards to also return `files` map. Design says mergeShards returns `{ errors, acs }`. Adding an extra key is a deviation... but consumers can ignore. Alternatively the gate re-reads shards itself.\n\nCleaner: have mergeShards return `{ errors, acs, files }` where files is ac → string[]. Design specifies `{ errors, acs }` — an extra field is additive, not a rename. I think that's acceptable and avoids duplicating shard parsing. But the design is explicit: \"`mergeShards({ root, index })` → `{ errors, acs }`\". A reviewer might flag the extra key.\n\nAlternative: gate re-reads <root>/test/traceability/*.json itself with a small loop. Duplication but no contract change. I'll do a tiny local helper in milestone-gate that collects covered files per AC (already-validated by mergeShards).\n\nActually simpler: add an exported `coveredFiles({root, index})`? That's a new name not in the design. Hmm, \"不要自行发明任何字段\". That refers to data fields mainly. I'll keep mergeShards as spec'd and add a private helper inside milestone-gate.\n\nLet me write a local function:\n```js\nfunction collectCoveredFiles(root) {\n  const map = new Map()\n  const dir = path.join(root, 'test', 'traceability')\n  let names = []\n  try { names = fs.readdirSync(dir).filter(n => n.endsWith('.json')) } catch { return map }\n  for (const name of names) {\n    let shard\n    try { shard = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(dir, name), 'utf8')) } catch { continue }\n    for (const entry of Array.isArray(shard?.entries) ? shard.entries : []) {\n      if (!entry || entry.status !== 'covered' || typeof entry.ac !== 'string') continue\n      const files = Array.isArray(entry.files) ? entry.files.filter(f => typeof f === 'string') : []\n      map.set(entry.ac, files)\n    }\n  }\n  return map\n}\n```\n\nGood.\n\nGate error shape: {id, detail} plus maybe ac/file. Output: `FAIL <id> <detail>`. A74-02 regex `gate\\.ac_not_covered[^\\n]*AC-026` → detail must include AC-026. I'll format `FAIL gate.ac_not_covered AC-026 status is planned`. So put AC first in detail.\n\nFor gate.trace_error: `FAIL gate.trace_error <ac/file> <detail>`.\n\nLet me settle on a single output line format for the gate: `FAIL ${id} ${detail}` where detail starts with the AC or file name.\n\n- gate.ac_not_covered: detail `AC-026 is planned`\n- defects.*: pass through as they come from checkDefects: those have {id, detail}; detail already starts with id (e.g., `a5-shell has no [fixed]`). A74-02 regex `defects\\.missing_fixed[^\\n]*a5-shell` ✓.\n- gate.run_failed: detail `full run exited N`\n- gate.manifest_not_full: detail mode\n- gate.file_not_executed: detail file path.\n\nThen final line `milestone-gate M1: PASS` / `BLOCKED (n errors)`.\n\nNow: for the gate, checkDefects errors are appended raw. Good.\n\nOrder: trace -> ac_not_covered -> defects -> run. Only run if all three empty.\n\nAlso `--milestone` required; missing → exit 2 (A74-06). ✓\n\nLet me write both files.\n\nOne more detail for check-defects CLI: `--milestone M9` → exit 2. Validate regex ^M[1-5]$ first.\n\nAlso the default mode when ledger absent prints the message and exits 0 — and should NOT print `check-defects: ok`. Design: \"默认模式下打印 `check-defects: defects.json absent, nothing to check` 并退出 0\". ✓\n\nNow writing check-defects.mjs.","signature":""}],"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b64c02387d24acacbd4a13028c46","_messageId":"01a1b6507d1e745295927c77c0e608ed","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b64c02387d24acacbd4a13028c46","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b6507d1e745295927c77c0e608ed","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b6507d1e745295927c77c0e608ed","codebuddy.ai/messageId":"01a1b650-7d1e-7452-9592-7c7903466bdd","traceparent":"00-1491732b1efa8226a936b146e12cfead-98331ebc19389995-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a1b64b-fe4d-73dd-9fb2-26f680d0b3a8,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a1b64c02387d24acacbd4a13028c46"},"__timestamp":"2026-11-07T14:01:48.723Z"}
