{"type":"user","uuid":"01a1b650-c3c5-7e07-b071-9e36a612fd13","session_id":"01a1b64b-fe4d-73dd-9fb2-26f680d0b3a8","message":{"content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_00_6cm6nExaHXOwS7afuZGf1675","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully created and wrote to new file: c:\\git\\dsh-CLIWorker\\.collab\\worktrees\\001\\scripts\\check-defects.mjs"}],"is_error":false}],"role":"user"},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b64c02387d24acacbd4a13028c46","_messageId":"01a1b6507d1e745295927c77c0e608ed","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b64c02387d24acacbd4a13028c46","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b6507d1e745295927c77c0e608ed","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b6507d1e745295927c77c0e608ed","traceparent":"00-1491732b1efa8226a936b146e12cfead-98331ebc19389995-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a1b64b-fe4d-73dd-9fb2-26f680d0b3a8,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a1b64c02387d24acacbd4a13028c46"},"__timestamp":"2026-11-07T14:01:48.743Z"}
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b650-c3d7-75e1-b32c-0efc5fb02d0c","session_id":"01a1b64b-fe4d-73dd-9fb2-26f680d0b3a8","message":{"id":"01a1b650c3d775e1b32c0efa5f6ce6c6","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now milestone-gate.mjs.\n\n```js\nimport fs, os, path, { spawnSync }, { fileURLToPath }\nimport { mergeShards } from './check-traceability.mjs'\nimport { checkDefects, milestoneRank } from './check-defects.mjs'\n```\n\nNote: importing check-defects triggers its main guard (false) ✓.\n\nGate:\n```js\nexport function runGate({ root, index, milestone }) {\n  const errors = []\n  const limit = milestoneRank(milestone)\n  const merged = mergeShards({ root, index })\n  for (const e of merged.errors) errors.push({ id: 'gate.trace_error', detail: `${e.ac ?? e.file ?? '-'} ${e.detail ?? ''}`.trim() })\n\n  for (const entry of index?.acs ?? []) {\n    if (!entry || typeof entry !== 'object') continue\n    if (milestoneRank(entry.milestone) > limit) continue\n    if (merged.acs[entry.ac] !== 'covered') errors.push({ id: 'gate.ac_not_covered', detail: `${entry.ac} is ${merged.acs[entry.ac] ?? 'planned'}` })\n  }\n\n  const defectResult = checkDefects({ root, index, milestone })\n  errors.push(...defectResult.errors)\n\n  if (errors.length > 0) return errors\n\n  // run\n  const coveredFiles = collectCoveredFiles(root)\n  const outDir = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), 'cliworker-gate-'))\n  let run\n  try {\n    run = spawnSync(process.execPath, [RUN_TESTS, '--root', root, '--out-dir', outDir], { cwd: root, encoding: 'utf8' })\n    const status = run.status\n    if (status !== 0) { errors.push({id:'gate.run_failed', detail:`full run exited ${status}`}) ; return errors }\n    let manifest = null\n    try { manifest = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(outDir,'files-executed.json'),'utf8')) } catch { manifest = null }\n    if (!manifest || manifest.mode !== 'full') errors.push({id:'gate.manifest_not_full', detail: `mode is ${manifest?.mode ?? 'missing'}`})\n    const executed = new Set(Array.isArray(manifest?.files) ? manifest.files : [])\n    for (const entry of index?.acs ?? []) {\n      if (!entry || milestoneRank(entry.milestone) > limit) continue\n      if (merged.acs[entry.ac] !== 'covered') continue\n      for (const file of coveredFiles.get(entry.ac) ?? []) {\n        if (!executed.has(file)) errors.push({id:'gate.file_not_executed', detail:`${file} (${entry.ac})`})\n      }\n    }\n  } finally {\n    fs.rmSync(outDir, {recursive:true, force:true})\n  }\n  return errors\n}\n```\n\nCareful: `spawnSync` with encoding utf8 — the child's stdio is piped, so node --test output is captured (not shown). Good, keeps gate output clean.\n\nHmm, but spawnSync's default maxBuffer is 1MB; test output could exceed for many tests. In fixtures, tiny. But if someone runs the gate on the real repo (T-009 will), the full run output might exceed 1MB. Set maxBuffer: 64MB.\n\nAlso timeout? No.\n\nNote: the nested run inherits CLIWORKER_RUN_ACTIVE=1 from an enclosing run; out-dir is a fresh mkdtemp → no guard trip.\n\nBut wait: there's a subtle issue in the fixture gate run under `npm test`. The parent test process has CLIWORKER_RESULTS_DIR=<parent dir>. spawnSync inherits env. run-tests sees outDir (mkdtemp) ≠ env dir → fine.\n\nAnother: for the fixture root, `findOrphans` in run-tests scans <root>/test — the fixture's test dir has unit/, traceability/, characterization/. traceability has no .test.mjs. characterization/defects/*.test.mjs — wait! test/characterization is one of the 7 enumerated dirs, so defects/a3-runner.test.mjs IS enumerated in the fixture run. Good, and it's a passing test (its body must pass). Let me make fixture defect tests trivially passing.\n\nCareful: in m2-planned, a5-shell.test.mjs has only `test('[repro] ...')` — a passing test. And a3-runner.test.mjs has `[repro]` and `[fixed]`. Both pass. So the full run has 2 files (test/unit/gate.test.mjs + the two defect files = 3). All pass. Manifest mode full. ✓\n\nAlso the gate run's manifest includes all enumerated; covered files recorded. ✓\n\nNow the CLI:\n```js\n--milestone required\n```\nOutput:\n```\nFAIL <id> <detail>\nmilestone-gate M1: PASS | BLOCKED (n errors)\n```\nExit 1 / 0.\n\nLet me write.\n\ncollectCoveredFiles local helper.\n\nAlso need `MILESTONE` comparator import from check-defects (milestoneRank). Fine.\n\nEdge: index unreadable → gate errors. I'll read index in main; if fails, push gate.trace_error? I'll just use {acs: []} and produce no ac errors — bad. Let's push a gate.trace_error 'index unreadable'. Keep it simple.\n\nWrite.","signature":""}],"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b64c02387d24acacbd4a13028c46","_messageId":"01a1b650c3d775e1b32c0efa5f6ce6c6","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b64c02387d24acacbd4a13028c46","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b650c3d775e1b32c0efa5f6ce6c6","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b650c3d775e1b32c0efa5f6ce6c6","codebuddy.ai/messageId":"01a1b650-c3d7-75e1-b32c-0efc5fb02d0c","traceparent":"00-1491732b1efa8226a936b146e12cfead-98331ebc19389995-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a1b64b-fe4d-73dd-9fb2-26f680d0b3a8,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a1b64c02387d24acacbd4a13028c46"},"__timestamp":"2026-11-07T14:02:01.943Z"}
