{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b651-5449-717f-bd69-666d4cd4316e","session_id":"01a1b64b-fe4d-73dd-9fb2-26f680d0b3a8","message":{"id":"01a1b6515449717fbd69666b3f7248ea","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now test/traceability/T-001.json.\n\nThen check-fast.mjs / .ps1, package.json, package-lock.json, tests, a3-runner, impl.md.\n\nT-001.json:\n```json\n{\n  \"task\": \"T-001\",\n  \"milestone\": \"M1\",\n  \"entries\": [\n    { \"ac\": \"AC-001\", \"status\": \"covered\", \"files\": [\"test/unit/runner-selftest.test.mjs\"] },\n    { \"ac\": \"AC-002\", ... },\n    { \"ac\": \"AC-003\", ... },\n    { \"ac\": \"AC-004\", \"files\": [\"test/unit/traceability.test.mjs\"] },\n    { \"ac\": \"AC-074\", \"files\": [\"test/unit/milestone-gate.test.mjs\"] }\n  ]\n}\n```\nT-01 expects `s.entries.map(...)` order AC-001,002,003,004,074 and keys [\"task\",\"milestone\",\"entries\"].\n\nWrite with compact entries.\n\nNow check-fast.mjs.\n\n```js\n#!/usr/bin/env node\nimport fs from 'node:fs'\nimport path from 'node:path'\nimport { spawnSync } from 'node:child_process'\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url'\n\nconst HERE = path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url))\nconst STEP_PATTERN = /^check-.*\\.mjs$/\nconst SELF = 'check-fast.mjs'\n\nfunction bytesCompare(a,b) { return a < b ? -1 : a > b ? 1 : 0 }\n\nfunction main() {\n  const dir = process.env.CLIWORKER_TEST_CHECK_DIR ? path.resolve(process.env.CLIWORKER_TEST_CHECK_DIR) : HERE\n  const finalScript = process.env.CLIWORKER_TEST_FINAL_SCRIPT ? path.resolve(process.env.CLIWORKER_TEST_FINAL_SCRIPT) : path.join(dir, 'run-tests.mjs')\n  if (process.env.CLIWORKER_TEST_CHECK_DIR || process.env.CLIWORKER_TEST_FINAL_SCRIPT) process.stderr.write('check-fast: test injection active\\n')\n  const cwd = path.dirname(dir) ... \n```\nHmm: \"子进程 cwd 为 `<dir>` 的上一级（仓库根）\". For the real case dir=scripts → parent=repo root ✓. For the injection case dir=temp → parent=temp's parent. Doesn't matter.\n\nWait — but `finalScript` when not injected = path.join(dir,'run-tests.mjs'); when dir is overridden but final not, that's odd but fine.\n\nList steps:\n```js\n  let entries = []\n  try { entries = fs.readdirSync(dir) } catch { entries = [] }\n  const steps = entries.filter(n => STEP_PATTERN.test(n) && n !== SELF).sort(bytesCompare)\n```\nNote: readdirSync gives file names; should ensure they're files. Add stat check isFile.\n\nThen:\n```js\n  for (const name of steps) {\n    process.stdout.write(`==> ${name}\\n`)\n    const r = spawnSync(process.execPath, [path.join(dir, name)], { cwd, stdio: 'inherit' })\n    if (!ok(r)) return fail(name, r)\n  }\n  process.stdout.write('==> npm test\\n')\n  const r = spawnSync(process.execPath, [finalScript], { cwd, stdio: 'inherit' })\n  if (!ok(r)) return fail('npm test', r)\n  process.stdout.write('check-fast: ok\\n')\n```\nA3-01 expects stderr contains `check-b.mjs`; the FAILED message uses step name. For the final step name = 'npm test'.\n\nExit code: `r.status === null ? 1 : r.status`.\n\nfail:\n```js\nfunction failStep(label, result) {\n  const code = result.status === null ? 1 : result.status\n  process.stderr.write(`check-fast: FAILED step ${label} (exit ${code})\\n`)\n  process.exitCode = code\n}\n```\n\nNote A3-01 `names=$($r.Out -match 'check-b\\.mjs')` where Out is stdout+stderr combined → the FAILED line is on stderr but captured. Also `==> check-b.mjs` is on stdout. ✓\n\nSort by code point: `a < b` string comparison is code-unit based. ✓\n\nShould stdout messages flush before spawn? process.stdout.write to a pipe is async... then spawnSync with stdio inherit blocks. Node buffers stdout when piped. Ordering could interleave weirdly but content is all there. To be safe use `fs.writeSync(1, ...)` for the step headers? That's synchronous and guarantees ordering before the child writes.\n\nActually with stdio:'inherit', the child writes to the same fd directly. If our stdout buffer hasn't flushed, child output may appear before the header. Order matters for A3-06's assertion \"输出里可见按字母序的 ==> ... 之后是 ==> npm test\". Let me use `fs.writeSync(1, text)` for headers — synchronous. Good.\n\nSimilarly final line. Use fs.writeSync(1,...).\n\nHmm, `fs.writeSync(1, ...)` works on Windows for stdout. Yes.\n\nBut careful: if stdout is a pipe and we writeSync, fine.\n\nLet me use a small helper `out(text)`.\n\nNow check-fast.ps1, 2 lines.\n\npackage.json modification.\n\nThen tests.\n\nLet me write check-fast first.","signature":""}],"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b64c02387d24acacbd4a13028c46","_messageId":"01a1b6515449717fbd69666b3f7248ea","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b64c02387d24acacbd4a13028c46","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b6515449717fbd69666b3f7248ea","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b6515449717fbd69666b3f7248ea","codebuddy.ai/messageId":"01a1b651-5449-717f-bd69-666d4cd4316e","traceparent":"00-1491732b1efa8226a936b146e12cfead-98331ebc19389995-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a1b64b-fe4d-73dd-9fb2-26f680d0b3a8,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a1b64c02387d24acacbd4a13028c46"},"__timestamp":"2026-11-07T14:02:36.155Z"}
