it — a problem! The extractTitles test I planned uses a source string containing `test('[AC-004] plain', ...)`. That's inside the test source file, so `Check-Traceability` for the repo will see... no, only files listed in shards are scanned. T-001 lists traceability.test.mjs for AC-004, and it looks for a plain title containing '[AC-004]' ✓.\n\nBut careful: my extractTitles test source has `test.skip('[AC-004] skipped', ...)` inside a *string literal*. extractTitles is called on that string at runtime, fine. But the file's own text also contains `test('[AC-004] plain', () => {})` as a string literal — would a plain regex scan of the file find titles inside strings? That's not used; only extractTitles over the file source for the shard check. extractTitles on traceability.test.mjs would match `test('[AC-004] plain', ...)` inside the string content too — but kind plain and contains [AC-004], so it counts as satisfying. It's already satisfied by the real test titles. Not a problem.\n\nCareful: A4-07 requires `--ac AC-004` to select only `test/unit/traceability.test.mjs`. ✓\n\nLet me write it.\n\nAlso for the graph test, I'll write a temp task-graph. Constructing from the index: tasks grouped by owner. Need `milestone` per task. Build:\n\n```js\nfunction buildTaskGraph(index, overrideOwner) {\n  const tasks = new Map()\n  for (const entry of index.acs) {\n    const id = entry.ac === 'AC-001' && overrideOwner ? overrideOwner : entry.owner\n    if (!tasks.has(id)) tasks.set(id, { id, milestone: entry.milestone, acceptance: [] })\n    tasks.get(id).acceptance.push(entry.ac)\n  }\n  ...\n}\n```\nHmm, if I override AC-001's owner to 'T-999' with milestone from AC-001 (M1), then:\n- owners.get('AC-001') = 'T-999' ≠ 'T-001' → graph.mismatch ✓\n- milestones.get('AC-001') = 'M1' = entry.milestone ✓\n- levels from acceptance entries; need to include levels per AC. I'll build `acceptance` array from index: {id, levels}. Then no level mismatch.\n\nThat gives exactly 1 mismatch. \n\nI'll write the graph to a temp file with fs.writeFileSync and pass `--task-graph`. Root = ROOT.\n\nBut careful: `--task-graph` plus `--root ROOT` → shard checks pass; index valid; graph mismatch 1 → exit 1. The test asserts `graph.mismatch` present. And a positive case: graph without override → no graph.mismatch, exit 0.\n\nHmm, but exit 0 requires no shard errors on the real repo — true.\n\nI'll do both in one test.\n\nWriting JSON to temp is fine.\n\nLet me write traceability.test.mjs.\n\nFor shard fixture id extraction, use --json and JSON.parse(result.stdout). Note: JSON output goes to stdout only. ✓\n\nAlso test that with `--json` on the duplicate fixture the id set is exactly the two.\n\nLet me write.","signature":""}],"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b64c02387d24acacbd4a13028c46","_messageId":"01a1b65228f67d7e93494a65b1c92fba","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b64c02387d24acacbd4a13028c46","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b65228f67d7e93494a65b1c92fba","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b65228f67d7e93494a65b1c92fba","codebuddy.ai/messageId":"01a1b652-28f6-7d7e-9349-4a6785f2155d","traceparent":"00-1491732b1efa8226a936b146e12cfead-98331ebc19389995-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a1b64b-fe4d-73dd-9fb2-26f680d0b3a8,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a1b64c02387d24acacbd4a13028c46"},"__timestamp":"2026-11-07T14:03:39.047Z"}
