{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b652-72d3-776d-9c89-6bb05b2a87b5","session_id":"01a1b64b-fe4d-73dd-9fb2-26f680d0b3a8","message":{"id":"01a1b65272d3776d9c896bae8c1d29bd","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Wait — a bug in the last test: `runJson(ROOT, ...)` passes `--index FIXTURE_INDEX` (since runJson hardcodes it) with `--root ROOT`. That's fine: the index is the same content as the real one, and shards come from ROOT/test/traceability. OK.\n\nBut careful: validateIndex is run on the fixture index — valid. Shards from ROOT — valid. Graph mismatch on AC-001 owner. ✓\n\nHowever, `runJson` asserts status; for the flagged case, status is 1 → fine.\n\nAnother issue: in the `build` function, task milestones: if AC-001's owner is overridden to T-999, T-999 gets milestone from AC-001 = M1; T-001 keeps AC-002..004 etc. But T-001's acceptance no longer includes AC-001. Then `owners.get('AC-001') = 'T-999'` ≠ 'T-001' → mismatch ✓. And milestone for AC-001 = 'M1' ✓ (T-999's milestone). No level mismatch (levels from acceptance array by ac). Result: exactly 1 mismatch. ✓\n\nNow `mergeShards` test asserts merged.errors empty. On ROOT, shards: T-001.json listing 5 covered, all files exist with titles (runner-selftest has [AC-001..003], traceability has [AC-004], milestone-gate has [AC-074]). ✓ — assuming those test files contain those titles. Yes.\n\nWait: AC-002 and AC-003 map to runner-selftest.test.mjs; titles exist ✓.\n\nNow milestone-gate.test.mjs.\n\n```js\nimport test from 'node:test'\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict'\nimport path from 'node:path'\nimport { spawnSync } from 'node:child_process'\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url'\nimport { extractTitles } from '../../scripts/check-traceability.mjs'\n\nconst HERE = ...\nconst ROOT = path.resolve(HERE,'..','..')\nconst GATE = path.join(ROOT,'scripts','milestone-gate.mjs')\nconst DEFECTS = path.join(ROOT,'scripts','check-defects.mjs')\nconst FIXTURES = path.join(ROOT,'test','fixtures','milestone-gate')\n\nfunction runGate(milestone, root) { return spawnSync(process.execPath, [GATE,'--milestone',milestone,'--root',root], {encoding:'utf8'}) }\nfunction runDefects(args) { return spawnSync(process.execPath, [DEFECTS, ...args], {encoding:'utf8'}) }\n```\n\nTests:\n1. m2-planned M1 PASS; M2 BLOCKED with both errors.\n2. m4-nocache M3 PASS; M4 BLOCKED with defect only, no gate.ac_not_covered.\n3. check-defects default: m2-planned exit 0; m4-nocache exit 1.\n4. check-defects --milestone: M1/M2/M5 on m2-planned.\n5. gate requires --milestone → exit 2.\n6. extractTitles [fixed]/[repro].\n\nCareful about the string 'gate.ac_not_covered' regex: `/gate\\.ac_not_covered/`.\n\nFor m4 M4: `assert.ok(!/gate\\.ac_not_covered/.test(out))`.\n\nLet me write.\n\nNote: these tests spawn the gate which spawns run-tests (nested). Works under npm test since out-dir is mkdtemp.\n\nAlso `test('[AC-074] ...')` for each.\n\nCareful: A1-03 expects `--ac AC-074` to select only this file. So no other file may contain '[AC-074]'. Check: traceability.test.mjs uses '[AC-004]'; runner-selftest uses AC-001/002/003; a3-runner has no AC tags; select none. ✓\n\nAlso T-001.json is not a test file. ✓\n\nLet me write milestone-gate.test.mjs.","signature":""}],"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b64c02387d24acacbd4a13028c46","_messageId":"01a1b65272d3776d9c896bae8c1d29bd","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b64c02387d24acacbd4a13028c46","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b65272d3776d9c896bae8c1d29bd","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b65272d3776d9c896bae8c1d29bd","codebuddy.ai/messageId":"01a1b652-72d3-776d-9c89-6bb05b2a87b5","traceparent":"00-1491732b1efa8226a936b146e12cfead-98331ebc19389995-01","baggage":"codeb