{"type":"user","uuid":"01a1b653-6975-7dc5-937b-91b4ac206b8a","session_id":"01a1b64b-fe4d-73dd-9fb2-26f680d0b3a8","message":{"content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_00_OLGoZylqbHFXasinr94R6128","content":[{"type":"text","text":" 270→  }\n 271→  fs.writeFileSync(skipsPath, '')\n 272→\n 273→  const mode = filtered ? 'filtered' : 'full'\n 274→  const env = {\n 275→    ...process.env,\n 276→    CLIWORKER_RUN_MODE: mode,\n 277→    CLIWORKER_RUN_FILTER: filtered ? options.acs.join(',') : '',\n 278→    CLIWORKER_ROOT: root,\n 279→    CLIWORKER_RESULTS_DIR: outDir,\n 280→    CLIWORKER_RUN_ACTIVE: '1',\n 281→  }\n 282→  if (options.updateSnapshots) env.CLIWORKER_UPDATE_SNAPSHOT = '1'\n 283→\n 284→  const args = [\n 285→    '--test',\n 286→    '--test-reporter=spec',\n 287→    '--test-reporter-destination=stdout',\n 288→    `--test-reporter=${REPORTER}`,\n 289→    `--test-reporter-destination=${manifestPath}`,\n 290→    ...files,\n 291→  ]\n 292→\n 293→  const result = await runNode(args, { cwd: root, stdio: 'inherit', env })\n 294→  let exitCode = result.code === null ? 1 : result.code\n 295→\n 296→  if (!filtered) {\n 297→    const manifest = readManifest(manifestPath)\n 298→    const verification = verifyFullRun({ enumerated: files, manifest })\n 299→    if (!verification.ok) {\n 300→      for (const error of verification.errors) {\n 301→        process.stdout.write(`FAIL ${error.id} ${error.path}\\n`)\n 302→      }\n 303→      if (exitCode === 0) exitCode = 1\n 304→    }\n 305→  }\n 306→\n 307→  process.stdout.write(`run-tests: ${mode} ${files.length} files, manifest ${manifestPath}\\n`)\n 308→  process.exitCode = exitCode\n 309→}\n 310→\n 311→const invokedDirectly =\n 312→  process.argv[1] && path.resolve(process.argv[1]).toLowerCase() === fileURLToPath(import.meta.url).toLowerCase()\n 313→\n 314→if (invokedDirectly) {\n 315→  main().catch((error) => {\n 316→    process.stderr.write(`run-tests: ${error && error.stack ? error.stack : String(error)}\\n`)\n 317→    process.exitCode = 1\n 318→  })\n 319→}\n 320→"}],"is_error":false}],"role":"user"},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b64c02387d24acacbd4a13028c46","_messageId":"01a1b6535fd97279b216c696550c94be","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b64c02387d24acacbd4a13028c46","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b6535fd97279b216c696550c94be","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b6535fd97279b216c696550c94be","traceparent":"00-1491732b1efa8226a936b146e12cfead-98331ebc19389995-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a1b64b-fe4d-73dd-9fb2-26f680d0b3a8,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a1b64c02387d24acacbd4a13028c46"},"__timestamp":"2026-11-07T14:04:42.230Z"}
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b653-6988-70b8-90de-3bd41aa925b1","session_id":"01a1b64b-fe4d-73dd-9fb2-26f680d0b3a8","message":{"id":"01a1b653698870b890de3bd2887061d6","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A concern: `env: { ...process.env, CLIWORKER_RUN_FILTER: '' }`. If Node drops empty env values on Windows, `process.env.CLIWORKER_RUN_FILTER` in the child is undefined, and my reporter fallback now yields '' when mode==='full'. Good.\n\nBut there's another Windows subtlety: `CLIWORKER_ROOT: root` where root may be `C:\\...` — fine.\n\nNow, one significant issue: **`--test-reporter-destination=stdout` combined with `stdio: 'inherit'`** — fine.\n\nAnother potential issue: Node's test runner runs files in child processes. Do the child test processes inherit `CLIWORKER_RUN_MODE` etc.? Yes. And does the *reporter* run in the parent runner process? Yes — the reporter runs in the process that node --test spawns as the \"test runner\" (the parent). It has the env we set since we spawned it with env. ✓\n\nNext: The reporter's `CLIWORKER_ROOT` — the parent runner process has it. ✓\n\nNow let me double check `check-test-discovery` single-point mode when `--root` is relative (A1-09 passes `$d` = 'test/fixtures/discovery-selftest/drift' relative). path.resolve → repo-relative to cwd. ✓ And `--manifest \"$d/manifest-ok.json\"` → resolved. ✓\n\nNow the full selftest in check-test-discovery: when it runs `runRunner(okRoot)`, `spawnSync(..., { encoding: 'utf8' })` with default cwd = process.cwd(). If someone runs `node scripts/check-test-discovery.mjs` from the repo root, cwd=repo ✓. If check-fast runs it with cwd=repo ✓. OK.\n\nBut what if cwd differs (e.g., gate runs it?) — no.\n\nNow: `check-test-discovery` imports `./run-tests.mjs` — that's fine.\n\nNext, I need to double check `check-test-discovery` prints nothing that would break `$r.Out -match 'check-test-discovery: ok'`. ✓\n\nNow let me think about the `[AC-001] the discovery self-test passes end to end` test: it runs check-test-discovery which itself runs `run-tests` on the ok fixture 2 times + findOrphans. Nested guard: parent env CLIWORKER_RUN_ACTIVE=1, results dir = parent's; out-dir from mkdtemp differs ✓.\n\nNow — WAIT. A critical problem! In `[AC-001] platformTest writes a cliworker.skip/v1 record`, I spawn `node probe.test.mjs` with env `CLIWORKER_RESULTS_DIR: dir`. But the parent env (under npm test) also has `CLIWORKER_RUN_ACTIVE=1`. Doesn't matter.\n\nAlso: under npm test, `CLIWORKER_ROOT` is set to the repo root, so record.file = path.relative(ROOT, tmpprobe) → contains '..' segments. My assertion `/probe\\.test\\.mjs$/` passes.\n\nNext: `test/unit/select.test.mjs` — the design says content is migrated verbatim. But it has unused imports `fs`, `os`, `path` — fine.\n\nNow a thought about `npm test` and the `test/unit/select.test.mjs` existing twice (old flat file still present). If I can't delete it, `npm test` fails with discovery.orphan. I'll report.\n\nLet me now also consider: does `check-fast` glob include `check-test-discovery.mjs`? Yes.\n\nNow let me write impl.md, then do a final consistency review.\n\nActually wait. There are a few more things to verify:\n\n1. `check-ci.mjs` — in the stale branch, `actual !== expected`. If the temp ci.yml has CRLF (copied from our LF file, so fine).\n\n2. A2-03: `(Select-String -Path $y -SimpleMatch 'needs:').Count` = 0. My ci.yml has no 'needs:'. ✓\n\n3. A2-02 `m.os.map(o=>o.name).join(',')` = 'ubuntu,windows,macos' ✓ (my matrix order). `m.node.join(',')` = '20,22' ✓.\n\n4. V-02: `Object.keys(require('./package-lock.json').packages)` = [''] → JSON.stringify gives `[\"\"]` ✓.\n\nWait — `node -p \"JSON.stringify(Object.keys(require('./package-lock.json').packages))\"` → `[\"\"]`. ✓\n\n5. package.json unchanged otherwise ✓.\n\nNow, `npm ci` in CI with our lockfile: lockfileVersion 3 and package.json has no deps. npm ci validates that package.json and lock agree on name/version. Should be fine.\n\nHmm, one risk: `npm ci` may complain \"Missing: ... from lock file\" — no deps. Or it may complain about `engines`/`license` mismatch? Not validated.\n\nNow let me think about whether `npm test` will actually pass given the runner passes explicit file paths to `node --test`. On Node 20/22, passing `.mjs` file paths works.\n\nOne risk: `--test` with explicit paths *and* the default test runner glob behavior for directories — not applicable.\n\nAnother risk: **Node 20 `--test` may not accept `--test-reporter` before files**? Order doesn't matter.\n\nAnother: if `files` is empty in a full run → `verifyFullRun` no_files error; but also `node --test` with no files would scan the whole cwd. We return early only for filtered. For a full run with zero enumerated, we'd spawn `node --test` with only reporter args → it would run its default glob over cwd! That could execute anything. Design says \"完整运行枚举为空。运行零个文件不得算通过\" → discovery.no_files. Better to not spawn when files.length === 0 in full mode: print FAIL discovery.no_files and exit 1.\n\nLet me add that: after computing files, if files.length === 0 → print `FAIL discovery.no_files` and exit 1 (for full). For filtered we already handle no_match.\n\nI'll add.\n\nAlso the arg-length check.\n\nLet me patch run-tests.mjs.\n\nAnother improvement: for `discovery.no_files`, verifyFullRun would also emit it; but we never get there. Add explicit handling.\n\nPatch: after the filtered/orphan branch, before length check:\n\n```js\n  if (files.length === 0) {\n    process.stdout.write('FAIL discovery.no_files\\n')\n    process.exitCode = 1\n    return\n  }\n```\n\nGood.\n\nNow, deeper thought on `verifyFullRun` when `enumerated` is `files` in full mode — the no_files check is redundant but harmless.\n\nNext: A1-07 orphan fixture: `run-tests --root orphan --out-dir $o` → findOrphans returns ['test/loose.test.mjs'] → prints FAIL discovery.orphan test/loose.test.mjs → exit 1 ✓.\n\nNow let me apply the patch.","signature":""}],"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b64c02387d24acacbd4a13028c46","_messageId":"01a1b653698870b890de3bd2887061d6","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b64c02387d24acacbd4a13028c46","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b653698870b890de3bd2887061d6","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b653698870b890de3bd2887061d6","codebuddy.ai/messageId":"01a1b653-6988-70b8-90de-3bd41aa925b1","traceparent":"00-1491732b1efa8226a936b146e12cfead-98331ebc19389995-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a1b64b-fe4d-73dd-9fb2-26f680d0b3a8,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a1b64c02387d24acacbd4a13028c46"},"__timestamp":"2026-11-07T14:04:53.147Z"}
