{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b653-9457-736e-a790-268e4538cb10","session_id":"01a1b64b-fe4d-73dd-9fb2-26f680d0b3a8","message":{"id":"01a1b6539457736ea790268c0baefc9e","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now, impl.md. But before that, let me do a final review of a couple of risky acceptance items I may have missed.\n\n**A1-13**: `Select-String -Path test/helpers/platform-gate.mjs -SimpleMatch 'cliworker.skip/v1','platformTest','recordSkip','satisfies'` — returns Pattern -Unique sorted → 4 lines. Our file has all 4 strings. ✓\n\n**A3-05**: `.ps1` non-empty non-comment lines ≤ 3 ✓.\n\n**A4-03**: `g('AC-008').levels` = ['contract','integration'] → join(',') → 'contract,integration' ✓.\n\n**A4-04**: `Object.keys(x.acs[0])` = 'ac,owner,milestone,levels,baseline' ✓.\n\n**T-01**: `JSON.stringify(Object.keys(s))` = `[\"task\",\"milestone\",\"entries\"]` ✓; entries map → `AC-001:covered:test/unit/runner-selftest.test.mjs;...` ✓; `s.entries.some(e=>'baseline' in e)` false ✓.\n\n**A4-02**: `--task-graph .collab/...` — my graph check compares owner/milestone/levels from the real task graph. The real graph's acceptance entries have `levels`, and tasks have `acceptance` + `milestone`. Should match my index. I verified the mapping by reading the graph's task list. Let me double check a couple of potentially mismatched levels: my index uses task-graph `acceptance` levels. Design's table also matches. One risk: AC-066 levels in the graph = ['e2e','integration'] and mine = ['e2e','integration'] ✓.\n\nAnother risk: AC-061 graph levels ['integration','unit'] and mine matches ✓ (line 455-458).\n\nAC-005: graph levels ['unit'] ✓.\n\nNow, does the graph contain a task for AC-038? T-029 acceptance ['AC-038','AC-069'] ✓ milestone M5 ✓ owner T-029 ✓.\n\nNow: graph check `levels` map built from `graph.acceptance` (all 74). Compare sets. My index levels for AC-072 = ['unit'] matches graph ✓.\n\nI'm fairly confident.\n\n**A4-02** exit 0 requires no other errors either. Real repo: index valid, shards valid... but shards valid only after select.test.mjs deletion? No—shards reference runner-selftest/traceability/milestone-gate which exist. ✓ So A4-02 passes regardless of select.test.mjs. Only A4-01 (covered=5 planned=69) also fine.\n\nWait, A4-01 expects 5 covered. My T-001.json has exactly 5 covered. ✓\n\n**A74-01** `run-tests --ac AC-074` → runs milestone-gate.test.mjs → its tests spawn the gate on fixtures. Those need run-tests to work. Should be OK.\n\n**T-02** full regression: `npm test` and `npm run check`.\n\nNow, `npm run check` runs check-ci, check-defects, check-test-discovery, check-traceability, then npm test. That's a full duplicate run of tests — slow but correct.\n\nPotential issue: check-fast's last step runs `run-tests.mjs` (not `npm test` literally) — design says implement as process.execPath run-tests.mjs, \"与 package.json 的 test 脚本等价\". ✓\n\nNow: **In check-fast, the final step inherits CLIWORKER_RUN_ACTIVE?** If check-fast is invoked from within a test (A3-01 etc.), the final script is the injected one, so no. In the real run (A3-06 / npm run check), CLIWORKER_RUN_ACTIVE is not set, fine.\n\nBut what about `npm test` → runner-selftest → check-fast (injected) → fine.\n\nAnother important one: **`check-defects` run by check-fast on the real repo** → absent → exit 0 with the message. ✓\n\n**`check-test-discovery` in check-fast** → selftest → requires no orphans (select.test.mjs deleted) and runs 3 nested runs. OK.\n\nNow let me consider **`test/fixtures/traceability/ac-index.json`** — it's inside a fixtures dir; run-tests ignores it. But `findOrphans` — top-level `test/fixtures` is skipped ✓.\n\nOne more: A5 - the acceptance also runs `git status` — I can't run git. My impl.md goes in .collab/tasks/001/impl.md.\n\nNow let me reconsider one risky item: **the `[AC-003]` pwsh platformTest block reads CHECK_FAST_PS1 and asserts**. Fine.\n\nBut hmm — `platformTest('[AC-003] the pwsh wrapper forwards...')` — extractTitles sees `platformTest(` with kind plain → satisfies traceability for AC-003 too (already satisfied by other plain tests).\n\nNow, a bigger concern: **`platformTest` is imported from `../helpers/platform-gate.mjs`** in runner-selftest.test.mjs. That file imports `node:test` and calls `test()` only inside platformTest. Fine.\n\nAnother concern: In runner-selftest, the `[AC-001] platformTest writes...` test constructs a probe file that imports platform-gate via `file://` URL. On Windows, `JSON.stringify(gateUrl)` produces `\"file:///C:/git/...\"` — valid inside an import statement. ✓\n\nNow think about whether `node probe.test.mjs` exits 0 when the only test is skipped. Node's test runner exits 0 if no failures. Yes.\n\nBut: the probe's `platformTest` calls `recordSkip` which writes to `dir/skips.jsonl`. Then t.skip(why). node:test's default reporter prints TAP. Exit 0.\n\nNext: **does `run()` pass `env` correctly in the probe case?** `{ ...process.env, CLIWORKER_RESULTS_DIR: dir }` ✓.\n\nNow, `Object.keys(record).sort()` — my record object literal order is schema, test, file, ac, requires, platform, node, reason, at. I assert the sorted array — must match exactly:\n['ac','at','file','node','platform','reason','requires','schema','test'] ✓ (9 keys).\n\nGood.\n\nNow let me write impl.md. It should state what changed, why, how to self-test, plus the Node 20 vs 22 observation request (design §3.5 says implementer must verify on both and record findings; I can't run anything, so I'll state that).\n\nAlso record the a3-runner assumption (design §11) and the delete blocker.\n\nLet me write impl.md at .collab/tasks/001/impl.md.\n\nActually — one more critical check. `check-traceability`'s `extractTitles` regex uses a lookbehind `(?<![\\w.])`. Node 20 supports lookbehind. ✓\n\nAnd `matchAll` requires the /g flag — present.\n\nOne more: `TITLE_RE` is a module-level regex with /g and used in `matchAll` via `text.matchAll(TITLE_RE)`. `matchAll` requires the global flag ✓ and does not mutate lastIndex? Actually String.prototype.matchAll clones the regex, so lastIndex of the original is preserved. Safe for repeated calls. ✓ (matchAll throws if the regex lacks /g; with /g it clones.)\n\nNow, `extractTitles` kind for `describe.skip`: match[3] = 'skip' ✓.\n\nNow the regex group numbering: `(test|it|describe|platformTest)` = 1; `(\\.(skip|todo|only))?` = 2; `(skip|todo|only)` = 3; `(['\"\\`])` = 4; `((?:\\\\.|(?!\\4).)*)` = 5. ✓\n\nCareful about the escaped quote inside `['\"\\`]` — in my source I wrote `(['\"`])` inside a regex literal within a .mjs file... Let me check what I actually wrote:\n\n```js\nconst TITLE_RE = /(?<![\\w.])(test|it|describe|platformTest)(\\.(skip|todo|only))?\\s*\\(\\s*(['\"`])((?:\\\\.|(?!\\4).)*)\\4/g\n```\n\nInside a regex literal, a backtick is fine (not a template literal). ✓\n\nNow `(?:\\\\.|(?!\\4).)*` — `\\\\.` matches a backslash followed by any char. ✓\n\nOK. Now `check-traceability` writes `FAIL` lines with `error.ac ?? error.file ?? '-'`. For index errors without ac, prints '-'.\n\nNow let me write impl.md.\n\nAlso should I worry that `impl.md` is inside `.collab/tasks/001` which the acceptance V-01 excludes ✓.\n\nLet me write a thorough but concise impl.md in Chinese (project docs are Chinese).\n\nContent:\n- 概述\n- 逐文件说明（改了什么、为什么）\n- 自测方法（命令）\n- 未完成/需人工的一步：删除 test/select.test.mjs\n- 设计未覆盖的判断与假设（a3-runner 缺陷推断；Node 20/22 reporter 观察未能在本环境执行）\n- 风险\n\nLet me write it now.\n\nOne more: brief says \"若 brief 指定了文档路径（例如验收报告），按约定在该文档追加小节\" — brief doesn't specify a doc path. So only impl.md.\n\nLet me write.","signature":""}],"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b64c02387d24acacbd4a13028c46","_messageId":"01a1b6539457736ea790268c0baefc9e","_meta":{"c