sn't emit \"# fail\", there's no non-zero failure count. The condition \"没有 `# fail` 之外的非零失败计数\" could be interpreted as: no non-zero failure count other than in `# fail`. If `# fail` is absent, then vacuously no `# fail` lines with non-zero. But they add \"（即 `# fail 0`）\" implying they expect to see `# fail 0`.\n\nThis is ambiguous. If they literally check output contains `# fail 0`, spec reporter fails. But the acceptance text is prose; the actual verification may be manual or by an automated checker. T-02 is described as a check on output. Risky.\n\nBut wait — Node 22 spec reporter output: Let me recall. Node v20+ spec reporter:\n```\n▶ [AC-001] ...\n  ✔ ... (1.2ms)\n...\nℹ tests 12\nℹ suites 0\nℹ pass 12\nℹ fail 0\nℹ cancelled 0\nℹ skipped 0\nℹ todo 0\nℹ duration_ms 123\n```\nSo no `# fail`.\n\nNode's default when `--test` without reporter is `spec` on TTY, `tap` when not TTY. But here we explicitly use spec for stdout. So output has `ℹ fail 0` not `# fail 0`.\n\nDesign §3.3 mandates `--test-reporter=spec` for stdout, so we must keep spec. The acceptance's T-02 wording may be sloppy. Since design takes precedence and design mandates spec, I'll keep spec. But this could be an acceptance failure if checked literally.\n\nCan I make `# fail 0` appear? Adding an extra reporter? No — design says exactly spec + files reporter. Adding a TAP reporter would violate \"字段名与 interfaces 一致\" and design's command. I shouldn't deviate.\n\nHmm. T-02's check might be done by a human/agent reading output. I'll keep spec (per design) and note in impl.md that spec reporter emits `ℹ fail 0` (Node 20/22), so the parenthetical `# fail 0` is satisfied in the sense that there is no non-zero failure count; if the reviewer requires the literal TAP line, that conflicts with design §3.3.\n\nActually, wait. Let me reconsider: perhaps acceptance was written expecting `# fail` because `node --test` with the *files* reporter? No.\n\nHmm, maybe the intended reading: \"输出中没有 `# fail` 之外的非零失败计数（即 