{"type":"user","uuid":"01a1b65f-026d-72fa-8747-94f85d54c0bb","session_id":"01a1b65d-b1c4-7fc0-a14a-b22b3e77b836","message":{"content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_00_Pw8DyhNjOEFSWzhRAqoE4341","content":[{"type":"text","text":"   1→#!/usr/bin/env node\n   2→// Verifies that .github/workflows/ci.yml is the current output of gen-ci.mjs for ci-matrix.json.\n   3→import fs from 'node:fs'\n   4→import path from 'node:path'\n   5→import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url'\n   6→\n   7→import { renderCi } from './gen-ci.mjs'\n   8→\n   9→const HERE = path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url))\n  10→const REPO_ROOT = path.resolve(HERE, '..')\n  11→\n  12→const EXPECTED_OS = ['macos', 'ubuntu', 'windows']\n  13→const EXPECTED_NODE = [20, 22]\n  14→const EXPECTED_ARTIFACTS = ['files-executed.json', 'skips.jsonl']\n  15→const CHECK_COMMAND = 'npm run check'\n  16→\n  17→function sortedCopy(value) {\n  18→  return Array.isArray(value) ? [...value].sort() : null\n  19→}\n  20→\n  21→function sameArray(actual, expected) {\n  22→  if (!Array.isArray(actual) || actual.length !== expected.length) return false\n  23→  return actual.every((item, i) => item === expected[i])\n  24→}\n  25→\n  26→function validateMatrix(matrix) {\n  27→  const problems = []\n  28→  if (!matrix || typeof matrix !== 'object' || Array.isArray(matrix)) {\n  29→    problems.push('matrix must be a JSON object')\n  30→    return problems\n  31→  }\n  32→\n  33→  const names = sortedCopy((Array.isArray(matrix.os) ? matrix.os : []).map((item) => item && item.name))\n  34→  if (!names || !sameArray(names, EXPECTED_OS)) {\n  35→    problems.push(`os names must be ${EXPECTED_OS.join('|')}`)\n  36→  }\n  37→  if (!sameArray(matrix.node, EXPECTED_NODE)) {\n  38→    problems.push(`node must be ${EXPECTED_NODE.join(',')}`)\n  39→  }\n  40→  if (matrix.check_command !== CHECK_COMMAND) {\n  41→    problems.push(`check_command must be \"${CHECK_COMMAND}\"`)\n  42→  }\n  43→  if (!sameArray(matrix.artifacts, EXPECTED_ARTIFACTS)) {\n  44→    problems.push(`artifacts must be ${EXPECTED_ARTIFACTS.join(',')}`)\n  45→  }\n  46→  if (!matrix.perf || matrix.perf.blocking !== false) {\n  47→    problems.push('perf.blocking must be false')\n  48→  }\n  49→  return problems\n  50→}\n  51→\n  52→export function checkCi(root = REPO_ROOT) {\n  53→  const errors = []\n  54→  const matrixFile = path.join(root, 'scripts', 'ci-matrix.json')\n  55→  const workflowFile = path.join(root, '.github', 'workflows', 'ci.yml')\n  56→\n  57→  let matrix = null\n  58→  try {\n  59→    matrix = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(matrixFile, 'utf8'))\n  60→  } catch {\n  61→    errors.push({ id: 'ci.matrix_invalid', detail: `cannot read ${matrixFile}` })\n  62→    return errors\n  63→  }\n  64→\n  65→  const problems = validateMatrix(matrix)\n  66→  if (problems.length > 0) {\n  67→    for (const problem of problems) errors.push({ id: 'ci.matrix_invalid', detail: problem })\n  68→    return errors\n  69→  }\n  70→\n  71→  let actual = null\n  72→  try {\n  73→    actual = fs.readFileSync(workflowFile, 'utf8')\n  74→  } catch {\n  75→    errors.push({ id: 'ci.missing', detail: '.github/workflows/ci.yml is missing' })\n  76→    return errors\n  77→  }\n  78→\n  79→  const expected = renderCi(matrix)\n  80→  if (actual !== expected) {\n  81→    errors.push({ id: 'ci.stale', detail: '.github/workflows/ci.yml is not the current generated output' })\n  82→  }\n  83→\n  84→  if (!expected.includes('continue-on-error: true')) {\n  85→    errors.push({ id: 'ci.perf_blocking', detail: 'perf job is missing continue-on-error: true' })\n  86→  }\n  87→  if (expected.includes('needs: perf')) {\n  88→    errors.push({ id: 'ci.perf_blocking', detail: 'a job depends on perf' })\n  89→  }\n  90→\n  91→  return errors\n  92→}\n  93→\n  94→function main() {\n  95→  const args = process.argv.slice(2)\n  96→  let root = REPO_ROOT\n  97→\n  98→  for (let i = 0; i < args.length; i += 1) {\n  99→    const flag = args[i]\n 100→    if (flag === '--root') {\n 101→      const value = args[i + 1]\n 102→      if (typeof value !== 'string' || value === '') {\n 103→        process.stderr.write('--root requires a directory\\n')\n 104→        process.exitCode = 2\n 105→        return\n 106→      }\n 107→      root = path.resolve(value)\n 108→      i += 1\n 109→    } else {\n 110→      process.stderr.write(`unknown argument: ${flag}\\nusage: node scripts/check-ci.mjs [--root <dir>]\\n`)\n 111→      process.exitCode = 2\n 112→      return\n 113→    }\n 114→  }\n 115→\n 116→  const errors = checkCi(root)\n 117→  if (errors.length === 0) {\n 118→    process.stdout.write('check-ci: ok\\n')\n 119→    process.exitCode = 0\n 120→    return\n 121→  }\n 122→  for (const error of errors) process.stdout.write(`FAIL ${error.id} ${error.detail}\\n`)\n 123→  process.stdout.write(`check-ci: FAILED (${errors.length} errors)\\n`)\n 124→  process.exitCode = 1\n 125→}\n 126→\n 127→const invokedDirectly =\n 128→  process.argv[1] && path.resolve(process.argv[1]).toLowerCase() === fileURLToPath(import.meta.url).toLowerCase()\n 129→\n 130→if (invokedDirectly) main()\n 131→"}],"is_error":false}],"role":"user"},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b65db5727ea58fa7ee2be908c6eb","_messageId":"01a1b65ef7747b488307b12f73955f9f","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b65db5727ea58fa7ee2be908c6eb","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b65ef7747b488307b12f73955f9f","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b65ef7747b488307b12f73955f9f","traceparent":"00-15ffef3552dd5d8b26c254c367358e26-0dddb10982c6d8a7-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a1b65d-b1c4-7fc0-a14a-b22b3e77b836,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a1b65db5727ea58fa7ee2be908c6eb"},"__timestamp":"2026-11-07T14:17:22.286Z"}
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b65f-0254-7aa9-82f2-ab5413c609ef","session_id":"01a1b65d-b1c4-7fc0-a14a-b22b3e77b836","message":{"id":"01a1b65f02547aa982f2ab52b33f1b0d","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A2-04: tampering with matrix using ConvertTo-Json produces reformatted JSON incl. `perf.blocking=true` etc. check-ci reads and validates → matrix_invalid. Good. For `$m.node = @(20)`, ConvertTo-Json of single-element array... In PS 7, `$m.node = @(20)` then ConvertTo-Json depth 8 → \"node\": [20]? Actually PowerShell may unwrap single-element arrays when assigning from JSON object property? `$m.node` is Object[] so fine, output `[20]`. Good.\n\nNote A2-04 clean case: copying matrix and ci.yml into temp; check-ci --root $t reads and compares renderCi(matrix) to file. Copy preserves content. Good, assuming matrix formatting doesn't matter.\n\nNow check-test-discovery and check-fast and fixtures + tests.","signature":""}],"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b65db5727ea58fa7ee2be908c6eb","_messageId":"01a1b65f02547aa982f2ab52b33f1b0d","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b65db5727ea58fa7ee2be908c6eb","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b65f02547aa982f2ab52b33f1b0d","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b65f02547aa982f2ab52b33f1b0d","codebuddy.ai/messageId":"01a1b65f-0254-7aa9-82f2-ab5413c609ef","traceparent":"00-15ffef3552dd5d8b26c254c367358e26-0dddb10982c6d8a7-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a1b65d-b1c4-7fc0-a14a-b22b3e77b836,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a1b65db5727ea58fa7ee2be908c6eb"},"__timestamp":"2026-11-07T14:17:25.507Z"}
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b65f-0f02-7acd-9f88-7ab4b92fe43f","session_id":"01a1b65d-b1c4-7fc0-a14a-b22b3e77b836","message":{"id":"01a1b65f02547aa982f2ab52b33f1b0d","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_00_xpNTNkXxI2qtyRzP5FLJ3960","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"C:\\git\\dsh-CLIWorker\\.collab\\worktrees\\001\\scripts\\check-test-discovery.mjs"}}],"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":82770,"output_tokens":244,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":81152,"cache_creation":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b65db5727ea58fa7ee2be908c6eb","_messageId":"01a1b65f02547aa982f2ab52b33f1b0d","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b65db5727ea58fa7ee2be908c6eb","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b65f02547aa982f2ab52b33f1b0d","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b65f02547aa982f2ab52b33f1b0d","traceparent":"00-15ffef3552dd5d8b26c254c367358e26-0dddb10982c6d8a7-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a1b65d-b1c4-7fc0-a14a-b22b3e77b836,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a1b65db5727ea58fa7ee2be908c6eb"},"__timestamp":"2026-11-07T14:17:25.507Z"}
{"type":"user","uuid":"01a1b65f-0f21-7097-b278-9b1ea169d2e0","session_id":"01a1b65d-b1c4-7fc0-a14a-b22b3e77b836","message":{"content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_00_xpNTNkXxI2qtyRzP5FLJ3960","content":[{"type":"text","text":"   1→#!/usr/bin/env node\n   2→// Self-test for the test discovery rules: proves the runner notices drift, that a filtered\n   3→// manifest cannot stand in for a full one, and that decoys and orphans are handled correctly.\n   4→import fs from 'node:fs'\n   5→import os from 'node:os'\n   6→import path from 'node:path'\n   7→import { spawnSync } from 'node:child_process'\n   8→import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url'\n   9→\n  10→import { enumerateTestFiles, findOrphans, verifyFullRun } from './run-tests.mjs'\n  11→\n  12→const HERE = path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url))\n  13→const REPO_ROOT = path.resolve(HERE, '..')\n  14→const RUN_TESTS = path.join(HERE, 'run-tests.mjs')\n  15→const FIXTURES = path.join(REPO_ROOT, 'test', 'fixtures', 'discovery-selftest')\n  16→const EXCLUDED_PREFIXES = ['test/fixtures/', 'test/helpers/', 'test/perf/']\n  17→\n  18→function printErrors(errors) {\n  19→  for (const error of errors) {\n  20→    process.stdout.write(`FAIL ${error.id} ${error.path ?? ''}`.trimEnd() + '\\n')\n  21→  }\n  22→}\n  23→\n  24→function checkRoot(root, manifestPath) {\n  25→  const errors = findOrphans(root).map((file) => ({ id: 'discovery.orphan', path: file }))\n  26→  if (manifestPath) {\n  27→    let manifest = null\n  28→    try {\n  29→      manifest = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(manifestPath, 'utf8'))\n  30→    } catch {\n  31→      manifest = null\n  32→    }\n  33→    const verification = verifyFullRun({ enumerated: enumerateTestFiles(root), manifest })\n  34→    errors.push(...verification.errors)\n  35→  }\n  36→  printErrors(errors)\n  37→  if (errors.length > 0) {\n  38→    process.exitCode = 1\n  39→    return\n  40→  }\n  41→  process.stdout.write('check-test-discovery: ok\\n')\n  42→}\n  43→\n  44→function runRunner(root) {\n  45→  const outDir = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), 'cliworker-discovery-'))\n  46→  const result = spawnSync(process.execPath, [RUN_TESTS, '--root', root, '--out-dir', outDir], {\n  47→    encoding: 'utf8',\n  48→  })\n  49→  const manifestPath = path.join(outDir, 'files-executed.json')\n  50→  let manifest = null\n  51→  try {\n  52→    manifest = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(manifestPath, 'utf8'))\n  53→  } catch {\n  54→    manifest = null\n  55→  }\n  56→  return { result, manifest, outDir, manifestPath }\n  57→}\n  58→\n  59→function runFiltered(root, ac) {\n  60→  const outDir = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), 'cliworker-discovery-'))\n  61→  const result = spawnSync(process.execPath, [RUN_TESTS, '--root', root, '--ac', ac, '--out-dir', outDir], {\n  62→    encoding: 'utf8',\n  63→  })\n  64→  let manifest = null\n  65→  try {\n  66→    manifest = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(outDir, 'files-executed.json'), 'utf8'))\n  67→  } catch {\n  68→    manifest = null\n  69→  }\n  70→  return { result, manifest, outDir }\n  71→}\n  72→\n  73→function selftest() {\n  74→  const problems = []\n  75→  const record = (message) => {\n  76→    problems.push(message)\n  77→    process.stdout.write(`FAIL ${message}\\n`)\n  78→  }\n  79→\n  80→  // 1. Live repository.\n  81→  for (const file of findOrphans(REPO_ROOT)) record(`discovery.orphan ${file}`)\n  82→  for (const file of enumerateTestFiles(REPO_ROOT)) {\n  83→    if (EXCLUDED_PREFIXES.some((prefix) => file.startsWith(prefix))) {\n  84→      record(`discovery.unexpected ${file}`)\n  85→    }\n  86→  }\n  87→\n  88→  // 2. Full run inside the ok fixture.\n  89→  const okRoot = path.join(FIXTURES, 'ok')\n  90→  const full = runRunner(okRoot)\n  91→  const expected = ['test/flows/c.test.mjs', 'test/integration/b.test.mjs', 'test/unit/a.test.mjs']\n  92→  if (full.result.status !== 0) {\n  93→    record(`discovery.selftest full run exited ${full.result.status} ${(full.result.stderr || '').trim()}`)\n  94→  }\n  95→  if (!full.manifest || full.manifest.mode !== 'full') {\n  96→    record('discovery.mode_not_full ok fixture manifest is not a full run')\n  97→  } else if (JSON.stringify(full.manifest.files) !== JSON.stringify(expected)) {\n  98→    record(`discovery.selftest ok fixture files ${JSON.stringify(full.manifest.files)}`)\n  99→  }\n 100→  fs.rmSync(full.outDir, { recursive: true, force: true })\n 101→\n 102→  // 3. Drift manifests.\n 103→  const driftRoot = path.join(FIXTURES, 'drift')\n 104→  const driftCases = [\n 105→    ['manifest-ok.json', null],\n 106→    ['manifest-missing.json', 'discovery.missing'],\n 107→    ['manifest-extra.json', 'discovery.unexpected'],\n 108→    ['manifest-filtered.json', 'discovery.mode_not_full'],\n 109→  ]\n 110→  for (const [name, expectedId] of driftCases) {\n 111→    let manifest = null\n 112→    try {\n 113→      manifest = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(driftRoot, name), 'utf8'))\n 114→    } catch {\n 115→      record(`discovery.selftest ${name} is not valid JSON`)\n 116→      continue\n 117→    }\n 118→    const verification = verifyFullRun({ enumerated: enumerateTestFiles(driftRoot), manifest })\n 119→    if (expectedId === null) {\n 120→      if (!verification.ok) record(`discovery.selftest ${name} should pass but reported ${verification.errors.map((e) => e.id).join(',')}`)\n 121→    } else if (!verification.errors.some((error) => error.id === expectedId)) {\n 122→      record(`discovery.selftest ${name} did not report ${expectedId}`)\n 123→    }\n 124→  }\n 125→\n 126→  // 4. Orphans.\n 127→  const orphanRoot = path.join(FIXTURES, 'orphan')\n 128→  const orphans = findOrphans(orphanRoot)\n 129→  if (!orphans.includes('test/loose.test.mjs')) {\n 130→    record(`discovery.orphan fixture missed test/loose.test.mjs (got ${JSON.stringify(orphans)})`)\n 131→  }\n 132→\n 133→  // 5. Filtered run does not compare.\n 134→  const filtered = runFiltered(okRoot, 'AC-001')\n 135→  if (filtered.result.status !== 0) {\n 136→    record(`discovery.selftest filtered run exited ${filtered.result.status} ${(filtered.result.stderr || '').trim()}`)\n 137→  }\n 138→  if (!filtered.manifest || filtered.manifest.mode !== 'filtered') {\n 139→    record('discovery.mode_not_full filtered fixture manifest is not filtered')\n 140→  } else if (filtered.manifest.files.length !== 1 || filtered.manifest.files[0] !== 'test/unit/a.test.mjs') {\n 141→    record(`discovery.selftest filtered files ${JSON.stringify(filtered.manifest.files)}`)\n 142→  }\n 143→  fs.rmSync(filtered.outDir, { recursive: true, force: true })\n 144→\n 145→  if (problems.length > 0) {\n 146→    process.exitCode = 1\n 147→    return\n 148→  }\n 149→  process.stdout.write('check-test-discovery: ok\\n')\n 150→}\n 151→\n 152→function main() {\n 153→  const args = process.argv.slice(2)\n 154→  let root = null\n 155→  let manifestPath = null\n 156→\n 157→  for (let i = 0; i < args.length; i += 1) {\n 158→    const flag = args[i]\n 159→    if (flag === '--root') {\n 160→      const value = args[i + 1]\n 161→      if (typeof value !== 'string' || value === '') {\n 162→        process.stderr.write('--root requires a directory\\n')\n 163→        process.exitCode = 2\n 164→        return\n 165→      }\n 166→      root = path.resolve(value)\n 167→      i += 1\n 168→    } else if (flag === '--manifest') {\n 169→      const value = args[i + 1]\n 170→      if (typeof value !== 'string' || value === '') {\n 171→        process.stderr.write('--manifest requires a file\\n')\n 172→        process.exitCode = 2\n 173→        return\n 174→      }\n 175→      manifestPath = path.resolve(value)\n 176→      i += 1\n 177→    } else {\n 178→      process.stderr.write(`unknown argument: ${flag}\\nusage: node scripts/check-test-discovery.mjs [--root <dir>] [--manifest <file>]\\n`)\n 179→      process.exitCode = 2\n 180→      return\n 181→    }\n 182→  }\n 183→\n 184→  if (root === null) {\n 185→    selftest()\n 186→    return\n 187→  }\n 188→  checkRoot(root, manifestPath)\n 189→}\n 190→\n 191→main()\n 192→"}],"is_error":false}],"role":"user"},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b65db5727ea58fa7ee2be908c6eb","_messageId":"01a1b65f02547aa982f2ab52b33f1b0d","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b65db5727ea58fa7ee2be908c6eb","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b65f02547aa982f2ab52b33f1b0d","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b65f02547aa982f2ab52b33f1b0d","traceparent":"00-15ffef3552dd5d8b26c254c367358e26-0dddb10982c6d8a7-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a1b65d-b1c4-7fc0-a14a-b22b3e77b836,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a1b65db5727ea58fa7ee2be908c6eb"},"__timestamp":"2026-11-07T14:17:25.537Z"}
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b65f-0f08-7773-83b2-efd035d57aa4","session_id":"01a1b65d-b1c4-7fc0-a14a-b22b3e77b836","message":{"id":"01a1b65f0f08777383b2efce1149dc1e","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Issue: `main()` is invoked unconditionally at the end (no invokedDirectly guard!). If a test imports this module, it runs selftest. Design doesn't require exporting from check-test-discovery, so maybe fine. But `check-defects` etc import check-traceability which has guard. check-test-discovery doesn't get imported anywhere (tests spawn it). OK.\n\nBug: check-test-discovery's selftest calls runRunner which spawns run-tests; when run via check-fast from a test? A1-08 runs it directly. runner-selftest also runs `check-test-discovery.mjs` via spawn (design §10 says check-test-discovery full selftest returns 0). Spawned from within npm test process → inherits NODE_TEST_CONTEXT → nested run would be blocked. Again fixed by stripping NODE_TEST_CONTEXT in run-tests (the grandchild). Good.\n\nAlso: `checkRoot` when `--root` given without manifest just checks orphans. A1-09 always passes manifest.\n\nWait: in the drift root, findOrphans enumerates test/unit/a,b and checks; no orphans. Then verify. Fine. `manifest-extra.json` includes a fixtures path; enumeration has 2 files; verify gives unexpected. Good.\n\nNow `runRunner(/ok fixture)` spawns run-tests with root=fixture. run-tests' output dir temp. Its mode full. It runs node --test on 3 fixture files. Fine.\n\nPotential problem: the reporter writes `platform`, `node` from child. Good.\n\nNow check-fast.","signature":""}],"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b65db5727ea58fa7ee2be908c6eb","_messageId":"01a1b65f0f08777383b2efce1149dc1e