{"type":"user","uuid":"01a1b65f-20b1-70dc-b991-c0e3699f6e83","session_id":"01a1b65d-b1c4-7fc0-a14a-b22b3e77b836","message":{"content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_00_xnhmoktmqWw3Zy1z32lH9206","content":[{"type":"text","text":"   1→#!/usr/bin/env node\n   2→// Runs every scripts/check-*.mjs in code point order (never itself) and then the full test run.\n   3→import fs from 'node:fs'\n   4→import path from 'node:path'\n   5→import { spawnSync } from 'node:child_process'\n   6→import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url'\n   7→\n   8→const HERE = path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url))\n   9→const STEP_PATTERN = /^check-.*\\.mjs$/\n  10→const SELF = 'check-fast.mjs'\n  11→\n  12→function out(text) {\n  13→  fs.writeSync(1, text)\n  14→}\n  15→\n  16→function err(text) {\n  17→  fs.writeSync(2, text)\n  18→}\n  19→\n  20→function byCodePoint(a, b) {\n  21→  if (a < b) return -1\n  22→  if (a > b) return 1\n  23→  return 0\n  24→}\n  25→\n  26→function stepFailed(label, result) {\n  27→  const code = result.status === null ? 1 : result.status\n  28→  err(`check-fast: FAILED step ${label} (exit ${code})\\n`)\n  29→  process.exitCode = code\n  30→}\n  31→\n  32→function main() {\n  33→  const injected = Boolean(process.env.CLIWORKER_TEST_CHECK_DIR || process.env.CLIWORKER_TEST_FINAL_SCRIPT)\n  34→  const dir = process.env.CLIWORKER_TEST_CHECK_DIR\n  35→    ? path.resolve(process.env.CLIWORKER_TEST_CHECK_DIR)\n  36→    : HERE\n  37→  const finalScript = process.env.CLIWORKER_TEST_FINAL_SCRIPT\n  38→    ? path.resolve(process.env.CLIWORKER_TEST_FINAL_SCRIPT)\n  39→    : path.join(dir, 'run-tests.mjs')\n  40→  const cwd = path.dirname(dir)\n  41→\n  42→  if (injected) err('check-fast: test injection active\\n')\n  43→\n  44→  let names = []\n  45→  try {\n  46→    names = fs.readdirSync(dir)\n  47→  } catch {\n  48→    names = []\n  49→  }\n  50→\n  51→  const steps = names\n  52→    .filter((name) => STEP_PATTERN.test(name) && name !== SELF)\n  53→    .filter((name) => {\n  54→      try {\n  55→        return fs.statSync(path.join(dir, name)).isFile()\n  56→      } catch {\n  57→        return false\n  58→      }\n  59→    })\n  60→    .sort(byCodePoint)\n  61→\n  62→  for (const name of steps) {\n  63→    out(`==> ${name}\\n`)\n  64→    const result = spawnSync(process.execPath, [path.join(dir, name)], { cwd, stdio: 'inherit' })\n  65→    if (result.status !== 0) {\n  66→      stepFailed(name, result)\n  67→      return\n  68→    }\n  69→  }\n  70→\n  71→  out('==> npm test\\n')\n  72→  const result = spawnSync(process.execPath, [finalScript], { cwd, stdio: 'inherit' })\n  73→  if (result.status !== 0) {\n  74→    stepFailed('npm test', result)\n  75→    return\n  76→  }\n  77→\n  78→  out('check-fast: ok\\n')\n  79→  process.exitCode = 0\n  80→}\n  81→\n  82→main()\n  83→"}],"is_error":false}],"role":"user"},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b65db5727ea58fa7ee2be908c6eb","_messageId":"01a1b65f0f08777383b2efce1149dc1e","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b65db5727ea58fa7ee2be908c6eb","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b65f0f08777383b2efce1149dc1e","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b65f0f08777383b2efce1149dc1e","traceparent":"00-15ffef3552dd5d8b26c254c367358e26-0dddb10982c6d8a7-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a1b65d-b1c4-7fc0-a14a-b22b3e77b836,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a1b65db5727ea58fa7ee2be908c6eb"},"__timestamp":"2026-11-07T14:17:30.033Z"}
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b65f-2091-7fb4-ae03-3eda63d65bee","session_id":"01a1b65d-b1c4-7fc0-a14a-b22b3e77b836","message":{"id":"01a1b65f20917fb4ae033ed809fafe15","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Design says final step `process.execPath <dir>/run-tests.mjs`, and \"`CLIWORKER_TEST_FINAL_SCRIPT` 覆盖最后一步的脚本路径\". Current code defaults finalScript to `path.join(dir, 'run-tests.mjs')` — good; uses `<dir>`, not repo root. But when dir=HERE, same.\n\nBut injection test A3-01: dir=$f (temp) containing check-a,b,c, final.mjs. finalScript env set to final.mjs. Steps sorted: check-a, check-b, check-c. But wait, `check-c.mjs` sorts after check-b; b exits 7 → stop. Good. Log a,b.\n\nA3-03: after rewriting check-b to success, and creating check-fast.mjs in $f (self file) → filtered by name !== SELF. Steps a,b,c; final. Log a,b,c,final. Good.\n\nFailure case in A3-02 via pwsh: env vars set in PS session propagate. check-fast.ps1 two lines. Good.\n\nNote: `spawnSync(process.execPath, [finalScript])` with cwd dir.parent = temp parent (C:\\Users\\...\\Temp). final.mjs writes CW_LOG via env. Fine.\n\n`stepFailed` uses result.status; if killed by signal status null → 1. Fine.\n\nNow, design says `==> <文件名>` printed to stdout; current out uses fs.writeSync(1). Fine.\n\nAlso design says if `CLIWORKER_TEST_CHECK_DIR` used, cwd = dir's parent. Fine.\n\nOne issue: design says final step is \"npm test\" implemented as `process.execPath <dir>/run-tests.mjs`; with injection, `<dir>` is the injected dir; current uses `path.join(dir,'run-tests.mjs')` unless env override. Good.\n\nNow read the tests.","signature":""}],"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b65db5727ea58fa7ee2be908c6eb","_messageId":"0